      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "A good idea to put into the constraints is an inverter, or when set below 0, data inverts.\n\ni have had a few things where i would've liked to use only one constraint, but was forced to use two due to not having the ability to invert the data from said constraint.\n\nAn example being, i want object A to move to the left, and for Object B to copy that movement, but to the right instead.",
